  "behaviour": "reset(z0_J=None) records status/label=no_feasible_budget, simulates nothing, invents no budget, and step() refuses"
 },
 "honest_findings": [
  "Measured mechanical work is 0.762-0.808 of the frozen power model's nominal cost over the same steps: in this regime the model over-predicts real work by 24-31%, so the internal budget runs out earlier than the measured energy would suggest. Both units are reported; neither is used as a proxy for the other.",
  "The nominal twin drifts 0.89-1.86 m from the actual robot in 8.5-16.8 s; the reference is never re-anchored, so this is real execution/model deviation, not a definitional zero.",
  "13-85 of every episode's steps are command-clipped: the learned policy saturates at the top of the vx domain, so its effective command is constant while its raw output varies.",
  "One episode (L2/full) crossed the nominal danger band for 55 steps without a physical collision: the nominal safety flag and the collision metric are separate, as the contract requires.",
  "All episodes end by budget_exhausted or stagnation within 8.5-16.8 s; no episode reached the goal at k=1.0. That is consistent with NAV-041's no_feasible_budget at k<=1.30 on the selection split, but this pilot is not a feasibility test."
 ],
 "limitations": [
  "one seed per method (deployment list lowest seed), one map instance per level",
  "no perturbation profile; clean-physics only",
  "single k (common-budget anchor 1.0), not a selected budget",
  "integration_pilot: wiring evidence only"
 ],
